      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113451,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113452,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113453,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 60% arise in the major salivary glands (typically the parotid gland) and 40% arise in the oral cavity (frequently the buccal mucosa) {22430772}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113454,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with a painless mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113455,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p >Sebaceous adenoma is rare, accounting for 0.1% of all salivary gland neoplasms and slightly less than 0.5% of all adenomas {31209701}. The mean age at initial clinical presentation is in the sixth decade of life (range: 22&ndash;90&nbsp;years), with an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 4:3 {22430772; 31209701}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:43:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113456,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113457,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113458,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours range in size from 4&nbsp;to 60&nbsp;mm in greatest dimension. They are commonly encapsulated or sharply circumscribed, varying in colour from greyish-white to pinkish-white to yellow or yellowish-grey {6704903}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113459,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are composed of closely associated dilated or microcystic salivary ducts with foci of prominent sebaceous differentiation, often with areas of squamous change. Atypia and pleomorphism are minimal; invasion of surrounding tissues is not found. Sebaceous glands vary markedly in tortuosity and size; they are frequently embedded in fibrous stroma. Marked oncocytic metaplasia may be found, and histiocytes and/or foreign body giant cells due to extravasated sebum can be seen focally. Lymphoid infiltrates and follicles, cytological atypia, necrosis, and mitoses are not compatible with a diagnosis of sebaceous adenoma {6704903; 22430772}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113460,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears are moderately cellular, with tissue fragments consisting of large epithelial cells with abundant foamy, finely granular or finely vacuolated sebaceous cytoplasm and centrally located bland round nuclei with slightly irregular nuclear contours and inconspicuous nucleoli {19670220; 31967730; 32926569}. Basaloid cells, squamous cells, and lymphocytes can be present, as well as histiocytes. Oncocytes are not seen. Necrosis, nuclear atypia, and mitotic figures are absent {7880973; 19697727}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113461,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:18:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113462,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 355,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> numerous closely packed sebaceous glands with minimal or no atypia, arising in salivary gland tissue.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:44:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
